+From 95fe7632f005ccec2384f2ba7a367e47d6ffcf86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: operator <225459632+operator@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:34:33 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 11/15] ricursive: prompt rows' partials at three ranks or more
+ by a row reduce-scatter (same bits, half the bytes)
+
+At four ranks each o_proj and down_proj gathered every rank's whole fp32 partial (three times a rank's share of
+bytes in, per exchange). cuda.rank_scatter sends each rank only its share of the rows, sums them in rank order with
+tf_rank_sum (the adds and order of tf_ripple_rank_sum), and the summed shares go to every rank in one send/recv group:
+half the bytes, the same bits. Prompt calls (more than 16 rows) at three ranks or more; TF_RICURSIVE_SCATTER=0 keeps
+the gather. Four GB10s: cold prefill 557-571 -> 643 tok/s at 7.6K tokens, 534-542 -> 610 at 30K; greedy replies
+byte-identical to the four-rank goldens (code, tool call, chat, a 7,240-token lookup; DFlash2 on).
