+Subject: [PATCH 12/15] ricursive: prompt projections by pfdense, prompt chunks
+ of 1,024 rows
+
+Prompt rows ran the EXL3 trellis kernel in 128-row blocks, decoding every rank's weights again each block (~30 TFLOPS
+on a GB10 at any chunk). pfdense (exl3_block/pfdense.cuh, DeepSeek-V4.1's fused prefill GEMM; built here for K2 10,
+the stored layout, as ricursive_pfd) decodes the trellis inside a tensor-core GEMM after exl3's rot_in: 39 TFLOPS on
+Ripple's four-rank shapes at 128 rows, 61-68 from 512. Prompt chunks grow to 1,024 rows (max_rows; the tap ring keeps a
+chunk plus 128). Decode rows keep the trellis kernel. TF_RICURSIVE_PFD=0 keeps it for prompts too (then every greedy
+golden is byte-identical to the four-rank build, and 16K WikiText-2 NLL bit-identical to 128-row chunks).
+
+pfdense does not add in the trellis kernel's order: on 16,384 WikiText-2 test tokens, one GB10, perplexity 6.9793 ->
+6.9802 (+0.013%), top-1 agreement 99.66%. Four GB10s with patch 0011: cold prefill 641 -> 1,051 tok/s at 7.6K tokens,
+610 -> 1,015 at 30K.
