+From a028db87096ad85faedd607e32e4d4bff2241f91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: operator <225459632+operator@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:25:39 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 13/15] ricursive: prompt calls' layer tails in two halves,
+ each half's sum overlapped with the other's compute (same bits)
+
+At four ranks the row-scatter sums were 28% of a prompt's GPU time on rank 0, run after the compute they wait for.
+A prompt call of 256 rows or more now runs o_proj through post_ffn in two row halves; each half's sum goes to a
+second, highest-priority stream behind an event while the other half computes, so only down_proj's second-half sum
+is waited out. Each row runs the same kernels on the same inputs, so the bits stay (greedy goldens byte-identical to
+the one-pass build). TF_RICURSIVE_OVERLAP=0 runs one pass. Four GB10s: cold prefill 1,038-1,051 -> 1,172-1,175 tok/s
+at 7.6K tokens, 1,015 -> 1,114-1,118 at 30K.
