+From 4f1dd4dc4ff6909d77aa1cbbf76595f978504bd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: operator <225459632+operator@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:55:53 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 15/15] lanes: shared rounds price a timed drafter pass by the
+ streams that draft, not as overhead every option pays
+
+A drafter that reports hold_costs (ricursive) has its pass timed at load, and observeOverhead splits a round's time
+into a fixed share and the pass. shared_drafts.budgets still priced allocation with overheadMs (fixed plus the
+measured pass), so a round drafting none was charged a pass it would not run: at 16 sampled streams on four GB10s
+plain looked like 16 / (75 + 77) ms against drafting's 28 / 187, and every round drafted (0.150 tokens a ms
+measured, against 0.191 for plain rounds). With hold costs it now passes fixedMs and the hold table to
+allocateDrafts, which prices the pass by the drafting streams and the deepest chain (as rule.budgets and headMs
+already do). TF_HOLD_SHARED=0 restores the old pricing. Families without hold_costs are unchanged.
+Replies unchanged (goldens identical to the previous build). Four GB10s, 16 x 128K, same binary A/B:
+prose (T 0.7) 16 streams 143.4 -> 190.3 tok/s, 8 streams 103.2 -> 112.0; SparkMan code decode 16 streams
+221.3 / 237.2 -> 221.1 / 238.4 (unchanged).
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
